Looking at greet.js:
```javascript
function greet(name) {
  if (!name || name.trim() === '') {
    return 'Welcome, friend!';
  }
  return `Welcome, ${name}!`;
}
```

So:
- `greet('Alice')` returns `'Welcome, Alice!'`
- `greet('')` returns `'Welcome, friend!'`
- `greet(null)` returns `'Welcome, friend!'` (because !name is true)
- `greet(undefined)` returns `'Welcome, friend!'` (because !name is true)
- `greet('Bob')` returns `'Welcome, Bob!'`
- `greet('Charlie')` returns `'Welcome, Charlie!'`
- `greet('Dr. Smith')` returns `'Welcome, Dr. Smith!'`

I'll update all the tests to use exact assertions.

